  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">JASS: Feminist Movement Buildning 3,0</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">JASS: Feminst Movement Buildning 3,0</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">JASS har ans&#xf6;kt till Sida om finansiering p&#xe5; 40 miljoner SEK som k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d till deras strategiska plan under 2020 till 2024.

Interventionen syftar till att bygga och st&#xe4;rka kvinnor&#xf6;relser, dvs. att utrusta och st&#xf6;dja kvinnor, aktivister och organisationer att organisera sig och st&#xe4;rka sin kapacitet att bidra till samh&#xe4;llsf&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndring och utmana oj&#xe4;mlikhet, diskriminering, v&#xe5;ld och milj&#xf6;f&#xf6;rst&#xf6;ring.
De konkreta aktiviteterna inkluderar;

1) Feministiska ledarskapsskolor och cirklar med utbildningsprogram som genomf&#xf6;rs p&#xe5; lokal, regional och global niv&#xe5; och som kombinerar m&#xf6;ten IRL med virtuella m&#xf6;ten. Utbildningsprogrammen finns p&#xe5; plats i Honduras, Guatemala, Mexiko, Malawi, Zimbabwe, Kambodja, Indonesien, Myanmar och Filippinerna. De t&#xe4;cker bland annat feministisk ekonomisk l&#xe4;skunnighet, proaktiva kommunikationsstrategier, personlig s&#xe4;kerhet. Inriktning och inneh&#xe5;ll baseras alltid p&#xe5; vad som &#xe4;r relevant och efterfr&#xe5;gat i varje land.

2) Mentorskap/ f&#xf6;ljeslagarverksamhet f&#xf6;r att bygga och st&#xe4;rka r&#xf6;relser och bidra till att st&#xf6;dja kvinnor och deras organisationer n&#xe4;r de tar p&#xe5; sig an politiskt sv&#xe5;ra fr&#xe5;gor. Denna typ av st&#xf6;d till kvinnor och deras organisationer g&#xf6;r det m&#xf6;jligt f&#xf6;r JASS att st&#xe4;rka lokala partners organisatoriska f&#xf6;rm&#xe5;ga att reagera p&#xe5; br&#xe5;dskande situationer som s&#xe4;tter s&#xe4;kerhet och f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjning f&#xf6;r aktivister och kvinnliga m&#xe4;nniskor&#xe4;ttsf&#xf6;rsvarare i fara.

JASS kommer att genomf&#xf6;ra interventionen genom sina regionkontor i Afrika, Latinamerika och Sydostasien samt med lokala partners.

Insatsens totala budget &#xe4;r cirka 34 miljoner USD f&#xf6;r fem&#xe5;rsperioden. JASS f&#xe5;r k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d bland annat fr&#xe5;n det nederl&#xe4;ndska utrikesministeriet, Novo Foundation, OAK Foundation och Open Society Foundation samt projektst&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n olika givare f&#xf6;r specifika lands- eller regionala program.

Finansieringen fr&#xe5;n Sida kommer att utg&#xf6;ra cirka 12-15% av den &#xe5;rliga budgeten.
Cirka 20% av den &#xe5;rliga budgeten kommer att vidarebefordras.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">JASS has applied to Sida for funding of 40 million SEK as core support to their strategic plan during 2020 to 2024. 

The intervention aims at movement building i.e. to equip and support grassroot women&apos;s activists and organizations to build and organize power and capacity to lead fundamental change policies, institutions and social norms to challenge inequality, discrimination, violence and environment destruction. 

The concrete activities include;
1) Feminist leadership Schools and Circles with training programs that are carried out on local regional and global level and that combine face to face convenings with virtual meetings. Training programs are in place in Honduras, Guatemala, Mexico, Malawi, Zimbabwe, Cambodia, Indonesia, Myanmar and Philippines. They cover feminist economic literacy, proactive communication strategies, personal safety and more. The setup, content and length is always based on what&apos;s relevant and requested in each country.

2) Political Accompaniment to build and strengthen movements and helps sustain women and their organizations as they take on critical agendas and build power. This type of support to women and their organizations allows JASS to strengthen the organizational capacity of local partners to respond to urgent situations that place the safety and livelihood of activists and women human rights defenders at risk.

JASS will implement the intervention through their regional offices in Africa, Latin America and Southeast Asia and with local partners.

The intervention&#x2019;s total budget is approximately 34 million USD for the 5 year period. JASS is getting core support also from the Dutch Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Novo Foundation, OAK Foundation and Open Society Foundation as well as project support from various donors for specific country or regional programs.

The funding from Sida will constitute approximately 12-15% of the annual budget.
 Approximately 20% of the annual budget will be forwarded as sub-grants.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the intervention is:
Strengthening womens activism, and cross-movement and cross-border networks for mutual protection and increased influence in the face of heightened political attacks against women on the frontlines.
&#xa0;
The specific objectives&#xa0; are:
1. Bolster womens leadership and organizing capacity through scaled up training and political education, including offering newly systematized methodologies on applied power analysis, movement strategy, political narratives, collective activist safety and wellbeing, as well as fresh content on economic, environmental and political justice.&#xa0;Build on and promote JASS We Rise toolkit through schools and webinars.&#xa0;
2. Build and fortify cross-issue, cross-border movement alliances and links  indigenous, environmental, feminist, human rights, LGBTI, workers, etc. within and across regions and in North-South exchanges  for greater political leverage, strategic collaboration, and safety.&#xa0;&#xa0;
3. Influence thinking, policy, practice and funding within the international human rights and development community to better integrate gender, power and collective approaches to protection.
4. Center grassroots women&apos;s innovations and demands, and amplify grassroots feminist contributions from the Global South through advocacy and creative use of social media, JASS Women Crossing the Line platform and the production of knowledge (e.g. articles, research, blogs, curated discussions) to influence understanding of, and responses to, violence and inequality.</narrative>
  </description>
